-- TESTS for Part 1 (definitions) and Part 4 (general conditions). Expected values come from
-- the Rules' own words and figures, worked by hand before the assertion was run; the money
-- in them is the fixtures' hypothetical money. Both sides of every threshold the two Parts
-- state. A failing assertion here is a finding, never a value to edit.
-- The 13 short-period assertions are generated from src:583-589 by tools/gen_shortrate.py.

§ `Tests — Parts 1 and 4`

§§ `Ages`
-- Born 15 June 1990: 35 the day before the birthday in 2026, 36 on it.
#ASSERT `the age in completed years, of someone born on` (YMD 1990 6 15) `, on` (YMD 2026 6 14) EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `the age in completed years, of someone born on` (YMD 1990 6 15) `, on` (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS 36
-- Born 29 February 2008: 17 on 28 February 2026, 18 on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `the age in completed years, of someone born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `, on` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `the age in completed years, of someone born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `, on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS 18

§§ `Part 4 clause 1 — who PTI insures`
-- The standard person and policy: insured.
#ASSERT `the insured person` `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` TRUE
-- Not living and working in Vietnam.
#ASSERT NOT (`a person who lives abroad` `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE)
-- 15 full days old on the first day of cover (1 January 2026): born 17 December 2025 yes,
-- born 18 December 2025 no.
#ASSERT (`a person born on` (YMD 2025 12 17)) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT ((`a person born on` (YMD 2025 12 18)) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE)
-- Up to 65 (fork F4: the whole of the 65th year). On 1 January 2026: born 2 January 1960
-- is 65, yes; born 1 January 1960 is 66, no; born 15 June 1960 is 65, yes.
#ASSERT (`a person born on` (YMD 1960 1 2)) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT ((`a person born on` (YMD 1960 1 1)) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a person born on` (YMD 1960 6 15)) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE
-- Mental illness and leprosy bar cover.
#ASSERT NOT ((`a person born in 1990 with mental illness:` TRUE `, leprosy:` FALSE `, epilepsy:` FALSE `, cancer:` FALSE `, disablement:` 0) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT ((`a person born in 1990 with mental illness:` FALSE `, leprosy:` TRUE `, epilepsy:` FALSE `, cancer:` FALSE `, disablement:` 0) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE)
-- Epilepsy bars Programme I only (fork F6).
#ASSERT NOT ((`a person born in 1990 with mental illness:` FALSE `, leprosy:` FALSE `, epilepsy:` TRUE `, cancer:` FALSE `, disablement:` 0) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` TRUE)
#ASSERT (`a person born in 1990 with mental illness:` FALSE `, leprosy:` FALSE `, epilepsy:` TRUE `, cancer:` FALSE `, disablement:` 0) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE
-- Cancer bars cover, except on continuous participation.
#ASSERT NOT ((`a person born in 1990 with mental illness:` FALSE `, leprosy:` FALSE `, epilepsy:` FALSE `, cancer:` TRUE `, disablement:` 0) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE)
#ASSERT (`a person born in 1990 with mental illness:` FALSE `, leprosy:` FALSE `, epilepsy:` FALSE `, cancer:` TRUE `, disablement:` 0) `is a person PTI insures under` (`a policy renewed continuously since 2023 on` `the full schedule`) `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE
-- Permanent disablement over 50%: 50 yes, 51 no.
#ASSERT (`a person born in 1990 with mental illness:` FALSE `, leprosy:` FALSE `, epilepsy:` FALSE `, cancer:` FALSE `, disablement:` 50) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT ((`a person born in 1990 with mental illness:` FALSE `, leprosy:` FALSE `, epilepsy:` FALSE `, cancer:` FALSE `, disablement:` 51) `is a person PTI insures under` `the standard policy` `, Programme I being in issue:` FALSE)

§§ `Definitions 4, 5, 7 and Part 4 clause 2 — the period and the start date`
-- Premium received 20 December 2025: cover from 1 January 2026 (the certificate's day).
#ASSERT `Part 4 clause 2: cover in the current period takes effect on` `the standard policy` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
-- Premium received 5 January 2026: cover from 00:00 on 6 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Part 4 clause 2: cover in the current period takes effect on` `a first-year policy paid late` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 6
#ASSERT NOT (`the period of insurance of` `a first-year policy paid late` `contains` (YMD 2026 1 5))
#ASSERT `the period of insurance of` `a first-year policy paid late` `contains` (YMD 2026 1 6)
#ASSERT `the period of insurance of` `the standard policy` `contains` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`the period of insurance of` `the standard policy` `contains` (YMD 2027 1 1))
-- Fork F3: continuous renewal measures from the date of joining; otherwise from the first
-- day of cover; definition 5 alone gives the first day of cover in both cases.
#ASSERT `the start date for waiting periods and exclusions, of` (`a policy renewed continuously since 2023 on` `the full schedule`) EQUALS YMD 2023 1 1
#ASSERT `the start date for waiting periods and exclusions, of` `the standard policy` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `the start date as definition 5 alone reads it, of` (`a policy renewed continuously since 2023 on` `the full schedule`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1

§§ `Definition 8 — waiting period`
-- 30 days counted from 1 January 2026: 30 January is the 30th day and is in it; 31 January
-- is not.
#ASSERT `a waiting period of` 30 `days, counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, contains` (YMD 2026 1 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`a waiting period of` 30 `days, counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, contains` (YMD 2026 1 31))
#ASSERT `the last day of a waiting period of` 30 `days, counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30
-- 365 days counted from 1 January 2026 end on 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day of a waiting period of` 365 `days, counted from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31

