§§ `Definition 13 and Part 2 B — checking a schedule`
#ASSERT `the schedule, checked against definition 13 and Part 2 B` `the full schedule` EQUALS RIGHT `the full schedule`
-- An optional benefit without Programme II.
#ASSERT `the schedule, checked against definition 13 and Part 2 B` (`a schedule with I:` TRUE `, II:` FALSE `, outpatient:` FALSE `, dental:` TRUE `, maternity:` FALSE `, income:` FALSE `, benefit 6:` FALSE `, Asia:` FALSE `, pre-existing:` FALSE `, special:` FALSE) EQUALS LEFT `an optional benefit was bought without Programme II`
-- Programme II sub-limits of 50+60+40+5+5+3+6 = 169m against a main limit of 200m pass;
-- raising benefit 1 to 82m makes 201m, which fails.
#ASSERT `the sum of the sub-limits of Programme II` `the Programme II cover` EQUALS 169_000_000
#ASSERT `the schedule, checked against definition 13 and Part 2 B` (`The schedule` WITH `Programme I` IS NOTHING, `Programme II` IS JUST (`the Programme II cover, with a benefit 1 limit of` 82_000_000), `optional benefit 1, extension to the countries of Asia` IS FALSE, `optional benefit 2, outpatient treatment` IS NOTHING, `benefit 3, dental treatment` IS NOTHING, `benefit 4, maternity and childbirth` IS NOTHING, `optional benefit 5, income allowance` IS NOTHING, `benefit 6, death and disablement from illness` IS NOTHING, `extended to cover pre-existing conditions` IS FALSE, `extended to cover special diseases` IS FALSE, `the waiting period for illness the contract states, in days` IS NOTHING) EQUALS LEFT `the sub-limits of Programme II add up to more than its main limit`
-- Programme I: sum insured 100m plus medical 20m = 120m against 120m passes; 121m fails.
#ASSERT `the sum of the sub-limits of Programme I` `the Programme I cover` EQUALS 120_000_000
#ASSERT `the schedule, checked against definition 13 and Part 2 B` (`The schedule` WITH `Programme I` IS JUST (`The Programme I cover` WITH `the sum insured` IS 100_000_000, `the main limit` IS 120_000_000, `the limit for medical expenses` IS 21_000_000), `Programme II` IS NOTHING, `optional benefit 1, extension to the countries of Asia` IS FALSE, `optional benefit 2, outpatient treatment` IS NOTHING, `benefit 3, dental treatment` IS NOTHING, `benefit 4, maternity and childbirth` IS NOTHING, `optional benefit 5, income allowance` IS NOTHING, `benefit 6, death and disablement from illness` IS NOTHING, `extended to cover pre-existing conditions` IS FALSE, `extended to cover special diseases` IS FALSE, `the waiting period for illness the contract states, in days` IS NOTHING) EQUALS LEFT `the sub-limits of Programme I add up to more than its main limit`

