-- Refunds on an annual premium of 12,000,000 with cover from 1 January 2026.
-- Cancelled 1 February 2026 (one full month): the scale keeps 1/4, so the premium for the
-- period not yet in effect is 9,000,000. PTI cancels: 100% of it. The insured person
-- cancels with no claim paid: 80%, 7,200,000; with a claim paid: nothing.
#ASSERT `the refund on` (`The cancellation` WITH `asked for by` IS `PTI`, `the date the written notice was sent` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `the date of cancellation` IS YMD 2026 2 1, `a claim was paid in the period of the present contract` IS FALSE, `a claim showed fraud, dishonesty or a scheme to profit` IS FALSE) `of` `the standard policy` EQUALS 9_000_000
#ASSERT `the refund on` (`The cancellation` WITH `asked for by` IS `PTI`, `the date the written notice was sent` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `the date of cancellation` IS YMD 2026 2 1, `a claim was paid in the period of the present contract` IS TRUE, `a claim showed fraud, dishonesty or a scheme to profit` IS FALSE) `of` `the standard policy` EQUALS 9_000_000
#ASSERT `the refund on` (`The cancellation` WITH `asked for by` IS `the policyholder or the insured person`, `the date the written notice was sent` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `the date of cancellation` IS YMD 2026 2 1, `a claim was paid in the period of the present contract` IS FALSE, `a claim showed fraud, dishonesty or a scheme to profit` IS FALSE) `of` `the standard policy` EQUALS 7_200_000
#ASSERT `the refund on` (`The cancellation` WITH `asked for by` IS `the policyholder or the insured person`, `the date the written notice was sent` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `the date of cancellation` IS YMD 2026 2 1, `a claim was paid in the period of the present contract` IS TRUE, `a claim showed fraud, dishonesty or a scheme to profit` IS FALSE) `of` `the standard policy` EQUALS 0
-- Fraud: cancelled at once, nothing refunded.
#ASSERT `the refund on` (`The cancellation` WITH `asked for by` IS `PTI`, `the date the written notice was sent` IS YMD 2026 2 1, `the date of cancellation` IS YMD 2026 2 1, `a claim was paid in the period of the present contract` IS FALSE, `a claim showed fraud, dishonesty or a scheme to profit` IS TRUE) `of` `the standard policy` EQUALS 0
-- Cancelled 1 July 2026 (six full months): the scale keeps 3/4; PTI refunds 3,000,000.
#ASSERT `the refund on` (`The cancellation` WITH `asked for by` IS `PTI`, `the date the written notice was sent` IS YMD 2026 6 1, `the date of cancellation` IS YMD 2026 7 1, `a claim was paid in the period of the present contract` IS FALSE, `a claim showed fraud, dishonesty or a scheme to profit` IS FALSE) `of` `the standard policy` EQUALS 3_000_000
-- Cancelled 2 September 2026 (over 8 months): the scale keeps it all; nothing to refund.
#ASSERT `the refund on` (`The cancellation` WITH `asked for by` IS `the policyholder or the insured person`, `the date the written notice was sent` IS YMD 2026 8 1, `the date of cancellation` IS YMD 2026 9 2, `a claim was paid in the period of the present contract` IS FALSE, `a claim showed fraud, dishonesty or a scheme to profit` IS FALSE) `of` `the standard policy` EQUALS 0

-- The certificate and card: returned on day 30, in time; not returned by day 31, a breach.
#TRACE `Part 4 clause 4: the insured person must return the certificate and the card` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insured person or the heir` DOES `return the certificate and the insurance card` AT 30
#TRACE `Part 4 clause 4: the insured person must return the certificate and the card` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)

§§ `Part 4 clause 5 — waiting periods`
#ASSERT `the waiting period for illness, in days, under` `the full schedule` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the waiting period for illness, in days, under` (`The schedule` WITH `Programme I` IS NOTHING, `Programme II` IS JUST `the Programme II cover`, `optional benefit 1, extension to the countries of Asia` IS FALSE, `optional benefit 2, outpatient treatment` IS NOTHING, `benefit 3, dental treatment` IS NOTHING, `benefit 4, maternity and childbirth` IS NOTHING, `optional benefit 5, income allowance` IS NOTHING, `benefit 6, death and disablement from illness` IS NOTHING, `extended to cover pre-existing conditions` IS FALSE, `extended to cover special diseases` IS FALSE, `the waiting period for illness the contract states, in days` IS JUST 60) EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `clause 5 treats as illness the event` `the standard illness event`
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 5 treats as illness the event` `the standard accident event`)

§§ `Part 4 clauses 6, 7, 9, 10, 11`
-- Clause 6: PTI would pay 8,000,000 on a cost of 10,000,000; another insurer pays 3,000,000;
-- PTI's limit 50,000,000 of 100,000,000 in all. Excess: min(8m, 10m - 3m) = 7,000,000.
-- Ratio: 8m x 50/100 = 4,000,000. Fork F21: the larger, 7,000,000.
#ASSERT `clause 6, the excess method: PTI pays, of` 8_000_000 `on a cost of` 10_000_000 `, given` (`Other insurance` WITH `the amount the other insurance pays` IS 3_000_000, `the limits of all the insurances, in total` IS 100_000_000) EQUALS 7_000_000
#ASSERT `clause 6, the ratio method: PTI pays, of` 8_000_000 `with a limit of` 50_000_000 `, given` (`Other insurance` WITH `the amount the other insurance pays` IS 3_000_000, `the limits of all the insurances, in total` IS 100_000_000) EQUALS 4_000_000
#ASSERT `clause 6: PTI pays, of` 8_000_000 `on a cost of` 10_000_000 `with a limit of` 50_000_000 `, given` (`Other insurance` WITH `the amount the other insurance pays` IS 3_000_000, `the limits of all the insurances, in total` IS 100_000_000) EQUALS 7_000_000
-- The other insurer pays 9,000,000: excess 1,000,000, ratio 4,000,000; the larger is the ratio.
#ASSERT `clause 6: PTI pays, of` 8_000_000 `on a cost of` 10_000_000 `with a limit of` 50_000_000 `, given` (`Other insurance` WITH `the amount the other insurance pays` IS 9_000_000, `the limits of all the insurances, in total` IS 100_000_000) EQUALS 4_000_000
-- Clause 7: a change of limits only on the renewal date.
#ASSERT `clause 7 accepts a change of limits on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `at` (`The renewal` WITH `the renewal date` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `the date the premium for the next period was paid in full` IS NOTHING, `PTI agreed otherwise to continue cover after the 65th birthday` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 7 accepts a change of limits on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `at` (`The renewal` WITH `the renewal date` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `the date the premium for the next period was paid in full` IS NOTHING, `PTI agreed otherwise to continue cover after the 65th birthday` IS FALSE))
-- Clause 9: subrogation up to what PTI paid.
#ASSERT `clause 9: the rights passed to PTI, on a payment of` 6_000_000 `against a recoverable` 10_000_000 EQUALS 6_000_000
#ASSERT `clause 9: the rights passed to PTI, on a payment of` 6_000_000 `against a recoverable` 4_000_000 EQUALS 4_000_000
-- Clause 10.
#ASSERT `clause 10: the medical dispute is settled` (`The medical dispute` WITH `the two experts agree` IS TRUE, `an arbitrator was appointed in writing by the two experts at the outset` IS FALSE) EQUALS `by the common opinion of the two medical experts`
#ASSERT `clause 10: the medical dispute is settled` (`The medical dispute` WITH `the two experts agree` IS FALSE, `an arbitrator was appointed in writing by the two experts at the outset` IS TRUE) EQUALS `by the arbitrator, whose decision is final and binding`
#ASSERT REFUSED `clause 10: the medical dispute is settled` (`The medical dispute` WITH `the two experts agree` IS FALSE, `an arbitrator was appointed in writing by the two experts at the outset` IS FALSE) BECAUSE "Part 4 clause 10 has no step when no arbitrator was appointed at the outset"
-- Clause 11.
#ASSERT `clause 11: the dispute is decided by` TRUE EQUALS `negotiation between the parties`
#ASSERT `clause 11: the dispute is decided by` FALSE EQUALS `a competent court in Vietnam, applying the law of Vietnam`
-- Clause 8: PTI's examination right, exercised.
#TRACE `Part 4 clause 8: PTI may have the insured person examined` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `PTI, the insurer` DOES `have the insured person examined by an independent medical establishment` AT 3
